{"name":"Irish Coffee","hex":"#62422b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coffee","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A beverage made by infusing the beans of the coffee plant in hot water. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A serving of this beverage."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale brown colour, like that of milk coffee.","Of a table: a small, low table suitable for people in lounge seating to put coffee cups on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coffee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Irish coffee","blocks":[{"text":"Irish coffee is a caffeinated alcoholic drink consisting of Irish whiskey, hot coffee and sugar, which has been stirred and topped with cream. The coffee is drunk through the cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Irish_coffee_glass.jpg/330px-Irish_coffee_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irish_coffee","wikidata":"Q622954"},{"title":"Irish Coffee (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Irish Coffee are a hard rock band from Aalst, East Flanders, Belgium, that officially started playing in 1970. They are best remembered for their single \"Masterpiece\" \nwhich made it to the Belgian charts. The band's music was a combination of hard rock and blues rock, with searing lead guitar parts and strong vocals. The band broke up in 1975 but reformed in 2002 with a new organist and bassist."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Irish_Coffee_-_2005_-_Dirk_Annemans.jpg/330px-Irish_Coffee_-_2005_-_Dirk_Annemans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irish_Coffee_(band)","wikidata":"Q2682118"},{"title":"Coffee","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a beverage brewed from roasted, ground coffee beans. Dark-colored and bitter, coffee has a stimulating effect on humans due to its caffeine content; however decaffeinated coffee is also commercially available. There are also various coffee substitutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg/330px-Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee","wikidata":"Q8486"},{"title":"Coffee (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a brownish color that is a representation of a roasted coffee bean. Different types of coffee beans have different colors when roasted—the color coffee represents an average."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_(color)","wikidata":"Q2932937"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Making_of_Irish_coffee_on_Coffee_Right_in_Brno%2C_Brno-City_District.jpg/500px-Making_of_Irish_coffee_on_Coffee_Right_in_Brno%2C_Brno-City_District.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Making_of_Irish_coffee_on_Coffee_Right_in_Brno%2C_Brno-City_District.jpg/1280px-Making_of_Irish_coffee_on_Coffee_Right_in_Brno%2C_Brno-City_District.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Making_of_Irish_coffee_on_Coffee_Right_in_Brno%2C_Brno-City_District.jpg/500px-Making_of_Irish_coffee_on_Coffee_Right_in_Brno%2C_Brno-City_District.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One method of adding the cream","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaking_of_Irish_coffee_on_Coffee_Right_in_Brno%2C_Czech_Republic.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Preparing_Irish_Coffee.jpg/500px-Preparing_Irish_Coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Preparing_Irish_Coffee.jpg/500px-Preparing_Irish_Coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gently running the cream over a spoon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APreparing_Irish_Coffee.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg/500px-Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg/1280px-Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg/500px-Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Green coffee describes the beans before roasting.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoffee_beans_unroasted.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/The_Vertue_of_the_COFFEE_Drink.jpg/330px-The_Vertue_of_the_COFFEE_Drink.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/The_Vertue_of_the_COFFEE_Drink.jpg/330px-The_Vertue_of_the_COFFEE_Drink.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 1652 handbill advertising coffee for sale in St. Michael's Alley, London","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Vertue_of_the_COFFEE_Drink.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Leo_Ruben%2C_1897%2C_Sarajevo.jpg/500px-Leo_Ruben%2C_1897%2C_Sarajevo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d